course: dictionary
lesson: 9297
title: Spearmint: a plant and a flavour
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spearmint is a common kind of mint plant with pointed leaves. It is also the fresh, sweet flavour made from those leaves. Context tells you which meaning is used: if the sentence is about gum, toothpaste or sweets, it means the flavour; if it is about a garden, it means the plant.
explain: «One version of carvone smells of spearmint, its mirror twin of caraway seeds.» Here spearmint means the smell or flavour. The clue is "smells of": you cannot smell a plant the way you smell a flavour. The sentence also tells you the two versions smell different, so spearmint is one smell and caraway is the other.
explain: Spearmint is milder and sweeter than peppermint. If a sentence says one gum is less strong than peppermint, you can work out that the spearmint one is the gentler flavour. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Spearmint is a common kind of mint plant with pointed leaves.
fact: The leaves have a fresh, sweet taste, and the flavour is used in chewing gum, toothpaste and sweets.
fact: Spearmint is milder and sweeter than peppermint.
fact: Spearmint is a herb that spreads quickly, so gardeners need to keep it under control.
fact: Spearmint is uncountable when it means the flavour, so we say "some spearmint", not "two spearmints".
exercise: «The gum tasted fresh and sweet, like spearmint.» What is spearmint in this sentence? | A pair of gloves | A large garden tool | A kind of sweet cake | *The flavour
exercise: Find and copy one word that describes the leaves of spearmint. | flavour | garden | *pointed | spreads
exercise: Spearmint is milder than peppermint. Which one is the stronger flavour? | *Peppermint | They are equally strong | Neither has a flavour | Spearmint
test: «Mum put spearmint toothpaste on the brush.» What does spearmint mean here? | Chewing gum | A park | *A fresh flavour in the toothpaste | A type of shoe
test: Which statement about spearmint is true? | Spearmint is a metal tool. | Spearmint is the strongest mint of all. | *Spearmint is a mint plant with pointed leaves. | Spearmint is a kind of bird.
exam: Which sentence uses spearmint to mean the flavour? | Spearmint spreads quickly in gardens. | The spearmint plant grew by the garden wall. | Spearmint has pointed leaves. | *The gum tasted of spearmint.
